.nh
.TH "PB-INBOX-DECLINE" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-inbox-decline - Decline an exact team file request


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb inbox decline <request-id> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Decline one pending team file request. The sender is told it was declined and cannot
deliver those files. --generation is optional: without it the command uses the request's
current generation.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--generation\fP=0
	expected request generation (default: the request's current one)

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for decline

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print JSON


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  pb inbox decline request_abc123
  pb inbox decline request_abc123 --json
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-inbox(1)\fP
